starting point idea:

```
"NewPort": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
     "Name": {
       "$ref": "#/$defs/Types/Name"
     },
     "ConnectsToName":  {
       "type": "string"
     },
     "PortType":  {
       "enum": {"PoweredBy", "Powering", "CooledBy", "Cooling"}
     },
     "Type":  {
       "const": "Port"
     }
  }
}
```

Now we will still need to see what is the upstream and downstream port or `containing` / `contained_by`, `powered_by` / `powering`.

Thats what `PortType` is for in that idea. It allows to express the relationship between the 2 components in a straightforward way.

Example:

```
{
    "Name": "PowerUnit1",
    "ConnectsToName": "Blade1Power",
    "PortType": "Powering",
    "Type": "Port"
}
```

then in some other config 

```
{
    "Name": "Blade1Power",
    "ConnectsToName": "PowerUnit1",
    "PortType": "PoweredBy",
    "Type": "Port"
}
```

Let me know what you think of this idea 😊 and if it applies to all use-cases you have in mind.
